  Provenance Audit
    Status: VERIFIED
    All four bins are submitted as null. The agent never completed its simulation pipeline—it was still waiting for the Pythia8 shower (stuck at ~22k/50k events) when the session ended. No values were fabricated or leaked; the nulls honestly reflect that the analysis step never ran.
    1 TRACEABLE

  Trajectory
    The agent demonstrated strong physics understanding and correctly set up a full MadGraph→Pythia8→Delphes→analysis pipeline for TChiWZ(550,200), but spent the majority of the session debugging HepMC3 format incompatibilities with Delphes and never completed the pipeline. The shower was at ~44% when the session ended, so no results were produced.
    A technically competent but incomplete run. The agent demonstrated strong physics judgment (correct signal identification, NLO cross sections, mass verification, proper VZ region cuts) and built a correct end-to-end simulation pipeline. However, it spent too much time debugging HepMC3 format issues and chose too large an event sample (50k) without estimating whether the pipeline could complete in the available time. The result is a null submission despite having all the components ready. The critical missing decision was to reduce N_gen when time was running short—even 5k events would have produced usable bin statistics for this signal.

  Strengths:
    - Correct physics: identified both charge-conjugate production channels and computed NLO cross sections
    - Caught and fixed MadGraph5 mass misconfiguration by comparing LO cross section to Prospino NLO
    - Persistent debugging of HepMC3 format issues through systematic testing with small event samples
    - Wrote a detailed analysis script implementing the full VZ region selection before needing it

  Creative moves:
    - Used small event samples (5, 50, 100 events) to debug the HepMC3/Delphes format incompatibility before committing to the full 50k-event run
    - Cross-checked MadGraph LO cross section against Prospino NLO to catch mass misconfiguration

  Stuck points:
    - Three iterations of shower.py to get a HepMC3 format that Delphes could read (missing vertex lines, then wrong vertex format, then missing beam particles for pyhepmc)
    - Running 50k events through Pythia8 shower took longer than the remaining session time, and the agent did not reduce N_gen or estimate completion time
    - Delphes repeatedly killed by shell timeout on the full event file

  Issues:
    - The session ended with no results submitted. The agent's pipeline was architecturally correct but never completed because the shower was still running. Reducing N_gen from 50k to 5k–10k would have been sufficient for 4-bin statistics and would have allowed the full pipeline to complete.
    - Multiple sleep-and-check cycles for Pythia8 and Delphes processes consumed context and time without advancing the work.
    - Report.md and datasets.yaml were left empty despite the agent having computed cross sections, identified datasets, and written analysis code. A future agent continuing this work would have no structured record of progress.

